From: immortalwrt-x86-64-fm350-pcie <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: wwan: t7xx: disable fraglist GRO on CCMNI

The FM350 CCMNI receive path has triggered malformed UDP fraglist GSO
packets that later reach skb_segment() and can crash the kernel.  Keep
ordinary GRO enabled, but do not allow fraglist GRO to be enabled on the
T7xx netdev until the modem receive path is proven to preserve the fraglist
invariants.

This is a device-specific containment measure for the FM350-GL PCIe build.

---
 drivers/net/wwan/t7xx/t7xx_netdev.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wwan/t7xx/t7xx_netdev.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wwan/t7xx/t7xx_netdev.c
@@ -158,10 +158,17 @@ static void t7xx_ccmni_tx_timeout(struct net_device *dev, unsigned int __always_unused txqueue)
 	if (atomic_read(&ccmni->usage) > 0)
 		netif_tx_wake_all_queues(dev);
 }
 
+static netdev_features_t t7xx_ccmni_fix_features(struct net_device *dev,
+						  netdev_features_t features)
+{
+	return features & ~NETIF_F_GRO_FRAGLIST;
+}
+
 static const struct net_device_ops ccmni_netdev_ops = {
 	.ndo_open	  = t7xx_ccmni_open,
 	.ndo_stop	  = t7xx_ccmni_close,
 	.ndo_start_xmit   = t7xx_ccmni_start_xmit,
 	.ndo_tx_timeout   = t7xx_ccmni_tx_timeout,
+	.ndo_fix_features = t7xx_ccmni_fix_features,
 };
